name: sim.addGraphStream
description: Adds or updates a graph stream. A graph stream is persistent, but can be removed with sim.destroyGraphCurve
luaSynopsis: int streamId = sim.addGraphStream(int graphHandle, string streamName, string unitStr = '', int options = 0, list color = [1, 0, 0], cyclicRange = 0)
pythonSynopsis: int streamId = sim.addGraphStream(int graphHandle, string streamName, string unitStr = '', int options = 0, float[3] color = {1, 0, 0}, cyclicRange = 0)
inputs:
1. graphHandle: handle of the graph
2. streamName: name of the stream
3. unitStr: string describing the unit of the stream. Can be None/nil
4. options: bit-coded:
    - if bit0 is set (1), the stream is not visible
    - if bit1 is set (2), the label is not visible
    - if bit2 is set (4), the points are not linked
5. color: rgb-triplet, with values between 0.0 and 1.0, indicating the color of the stream. Can be None/nil
6. cyclicRange: can be used with cyclic values (e.g. angles) for correct data interpretation during stream data transformation. Set to 0 if not used
outputs:
1. streamId: id of the created/updated stream
